      "description": "**Role:** HTTP entry point; deserializes the cart and kicks off the pipeline.\n**Risk:** new public API surface\n\n**Discussion:** should this endpoint require an idempotency key to prevent a duplicate checkout on client retry? (🟡 Significant)\n\n**Outcome:** Open discussion — tracked separately as IDEMPOTENCY-142, out of scope for this PR."
    },
    {
      "title": "2/6: OrderValidator",
      "file": "src/Orders/OrderValidator.cs",
      "line": 12,
      "description": "No concerns — empty-cart and quantity checks confirmed. (Internal helper, low risk.)"
    },
    {
      "title": "3/6: InventoryReservationService",
      "file": "src/Inventory/InventoryReservationService.cs",
      "line": 30,
      "description": "**Role:** Reserves stock for each line item; the branch point that decides reserved vs. out-of-stock.\n**Risk:** concurrency-sensitive, shared state\n\n**Discussion:** under concurrent checkouts for the same SKU, can two requests both read stock before either decrements it, over-reserving? (🔴 Blocking)\n\n**Outcome:** Applied — replaced the read-then-write with a single conditional UPDATE statement, branching on rows-affected. Commit `c4d5e6f`."
    },
    {
      "title": "4/6: PricingService",
      "file": "src/Pricing/PricingService.cs",
      "line": 40,
      "description": "**Role:** Computes the order total from reserved line items, applying discounts before tax.\n**Risk:** touches money\n\n**Discussion:** should the rounding mode be explicit, given this is a financial total? (⚪ Minor)\n\n**Outcome:** Applied — changed to `Math.Round(total, 2, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero)`. Commit `c4d5e6f`."
    },
    {
      "title": "5/6: OrderRepository",
      "file": "src/Data/OrderRepository.cs",
      "line": 25,
      "description": "**Role:** Persists the order and its inventory reservation together.\n**Risk:** data integrity\n\nNo concerns — order and reservation writes confirmed wrapped in one `TransactionScope`. Kept as a full step, not collapsed, because this component is high-risk even though it's clean (see principles.md, \"Collapse the clean ones, but not the risky ones\")."
    },
